  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>According to the town hall, La Londe-les-Maures has three concession beaches (Miramar, Tamaris, Argentière), plus the non-concession beaches of Pellegrin and Pansard, nearly 3 km of fine sand in all. The lifeguard posts at Miramar, Tamaris and Argentière are open daily during the supervision season (2 July to 30 August in 2026). The town hall names no "Bormettes beach": that name refers to a neighbourhood of the town around the old factory and its theatre, not to a beach.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Several unofficial guides (France 3 Régions 2023, Nice-Matin, EmmèneTonChien) cite a dog area between Tamaris beach and Argentière beach, marked by "Dog area" signs according to Nice-Matin. The regional Provence-Alpes-Côte d'Azur Tourisme site lists a "dog beach" among the beaches of La Londe-les-Maures and says it is open to dogs. The extracts read from the town hall's "Les plages" page do not mention dogs, and the beach policing rules dated 12 June 2025, published by the town hall as a PDF, could not be read: the exact rule (leash, hours, season) is therefore not confirmed.</p>
      <p>Sources differ on the details. Nice-Matin describes an area where dogs can run off the leash, with free parking at Argentière to reach the path between the two beaches; France 3 Régions speaks of a beach "in front of the Bormettes factory"; the Plages.tv site describes a very narrow strip, more of a water-access point than a beach to settle on. EmmèneTonChien (updated 9 June 2026) says Argentière itself no longer accepts dogs and that only the stretch between Tamaris and Argentière is tolerated, while other guides present it as a dog zone open all year: none of these claims is confirmed by the town hall. Summer hours or dog showers mentioned by guides are not confirmed either.</p>
      <p><strong>Worth checking before you go</strong>: summer hours and leash rule (2025 beach policing rules not read), whether the showers exist, and the status of Argentière itself.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: stay outside the supervised swimming areas and keep your dog on a leash, as a precaution.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Miramar, Tamaris and Argentière beaches are next to the area; the town hall also mentions a coastal path reachable from the beaches. Dog access conditions for these beaches and this path are not specified in the extracts read.</p>
    </div>

